## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design automated degradation with controlled risk during external dependency pressure and multi-region operation.

## Key Concepts
- Circuit breakers and failover
- Per-region degradation strategies
- Idempotent queues and exactly-once delivery
- Canary and synthetic testing
- Rollback criteria and observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for circuit breaker state machine
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold, resetTime) {
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.resetTime = resetTime;
    this.failures = 0;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
  }
  onFailure() {
    this.failures++;
    if (this.failures > this.threshold) this.state = 'OPEN';
  }
  canRequest() { return this.state !== 'OPEN'; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for multi-tenant services with mixed SLIs?
- How would you validate degradation paths in canaries without impacting customers?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design scalable alerting that reduces noise while preserving critical signals, across multi-region K8s clusters, using common tools, with safe rollout.

## Key Concepts
- Alert routing and deduplication (Alertmanager, labels)
- Global blackout policy with per-region windows
- Canary rollout for rule changes; staging validation
- Metrics: alert rate, MTTA, MTTR, missed-incident risk; rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple in-memory alert suppression
const suppression = new Map(); // key -> timestamp until which alerts are muted
function shouldAlert(key) {
  const t = suppression.get(key);
  if (!t) return true;
  return Date.now() > t;
}
function suppress(key, durationMs) {
  suppression.set(key, Date.now() + durationMs);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for cross-cloud regions with drift?
- How would you validate that suppression does not hide critical incidents during outages?

